<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasan al-Kalbi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 964</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Kalbi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasan al-Kalbi was the first emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalbid-dynasty">Kalbid dynasty</a>, appointed by the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mansur in 948 to restore order on the island. He suppressed revolts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a>, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> and founded a hereditary line that ruled Sicily under Fatimid overlordship until the 1050s.</p></div>
